(version 1)

# IEEE 802.3at requires 1500 Vrms isolation between the cable-side power
# interface and the device circuitry. That is a surge / ground-potential
# requirement, not a shock-hazard one: 57 V DC is below the 60 V ES1
# threshold of IEC 62368-1. 1500 Vrms across a PCB gap needs ~2 mm.
#
# The POE class is the PRIMARY (cable) side only: POE_TAP_A1/A2/B1/B2 and
# POE_VIN_P/N. Note +5V_POE is the DP9900's ISOLATED OUTPUT despite its
# name and is deliberately NOT in this class.
#
# Scoped to POE-vs-non-POE so that normal spacing still applies between the
# primary-side nets themselves.
#
# TWO-TIER, and the reason matters:
#
# Inside J2 the isolation barrier is the magjack's own transformer, not the
# PCB. The HR871150C brings the cable-side centre taps (pins 7-10) out on
# 2.54 mm pitch alongside the PHY-side MDI pins (1-5), so J2.5 ETH_RXN sits
# 1.016 mm from J2.7 POE_TAP_A1 by the connector's construction. A 2 mm PCB
# rule there is unsatisfiable by any layout, and it would also forbid routing
# the MDI pairs out of the connector at all. Holding the board to 2 mm when
# the qualified connector achieves 1.016 mm buys no safety margin, because
# the connector is in parallel with the board and already sets the limit.
#
# So: 2 mm everywhere the layout controls the gap, and 1 mm within J2's pin
# field, which is still no worse than the connector's own spacing. The real
# barrier -- the plane keep-out under the primary-side copper -- is unaffected
# and remains mandatory (see .konnect/project.json design rules).

(rule "PoE isolation barrier"
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'POE' && B.NetClass != 'POE' && !A.memberOfFootprint('J2')")
	(constraint clearance (min 2mm)))

(rule "PoE isolation barrier at magjack"
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'POE' && B.NetClass != 'POE' && A.memberOfFootprint('J2')")
	(constraint clearance (min 1mm)))

# USB-C J3 (TYPE-C-31-M-12) is a dense Type-C footprint. The spacing between
# its own pads (GND/VBUS/CC/SBU) and their shared solder-mask openings is set
# by the connector, not by the layout, so intra-connector clearance is not a
# layout defect. Scope strictly to pad pairs that both belong to J3.
(rule "J3 USB-C internal clearance"
	(condition "A.memberOfFootprint('J3') && B.memberOfFootprint('J3')")
	(constraint clearance (min 0mm)))

# Mechanical / shield plated holes carry no net: the HR871150C (J2) cable-side
# locating posts, the USB-C (J3) shield posts, and the M3 mounting holes. Their
# annular ring is a mechanical feature, not a current path. Waive the annular
# minimum for PLATED, NO-NET holes only, so signal through-hole pins (which
# have a net) are still fully checked.
(rule "Mechanical hole annular"
	(condition "A.isPlated() && A.NetName == ''")
	(constraint annular_width (min 0mm)))
